; The one line that makes the lever legible. The board is a physical order
; instrument: throwing it is what actually sends a train, and it does not
; check the copy against the paper. Players read the old header as a menu of
; routes that must match the telegram; this says the opposite in the object's
; own voice, without a tutorial box.
;
; It sits in the bare slate band under the header card (card bottom strip ends
; at y 0.982, the MAIN label starts at 0.90), never over the diagram, and it is
; short enough to clear the slate's 0.72 m width at this pixel size.
[node name="InstructionLabel3D" type="Label3D" parent="."]
position = Vector3(0, 0.958, -0.048)
rotation = Vector3(0, 3.141593, 0)
pixel_size = 0.0024
modulate = Color(0.68, 0.62, 0.48, 1)
outline_size = 0
text = "THROW = SEND. IT DOES NOT READ THE COPY."
font_size = 12
font_size = 11

